From: justririll/x1e-sleep <x1e-sleep@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: syscon: skip the parent clock of clock providers

Taken from justririll/x1e-sleep kernel/sleep/. SM8550 TCSR is "qcom,sm8550-tcsr", "syscon"
with clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK> and #clock-cells, so syscon keeps bi_tcxo (the
sleep-set XO vote) prepared forever, which keeps AOP from turning the crystal off.
---
--- a/drivers/mfd/syscon.c	2026-09-29 07:29:46.620377869 +0300
+++ b/drivers/mfd/syscon.c	2026-09-29 07:29:46.657377043 +0300
@@ -123,7 +123,16 @@
 	}
 
 	if (check_res) {
-		clk = of_clk_get(np, 0);
+		/*
+		 * The "clocks" of a clock provider (e.g. the X1E TCSR block) are
+		 * its parent clocks, not a register clock. Attaching one keeps it
+		 * prepared forever, which pins an RPMh XO vote and blocks the SoC
+		 * from turning the crystal off in suspend.
+		 */
+		if (of_property_present(np, "#clock-cells"))
+			clk = ERR_PTR(-ENOENT);
+		else
+			clk = of_clk_get(np, 0);
 		if (IS_ERR(clk)) {
 			ret = PTR_ERR(clk);
 			/* clock is optional */
